GATEWAY LOG AVAILABILITY
========================

The generic gateway detail Logs tab reads the system and firewall REST endpoints.
It does not consume the separate live SSE endpoint and makes no continuous-delivery
or instant client-side revocation guarantee.

Only a successful response with the selected gateway ID, matching vendor and a
bounded array of at most the requested200 row objects can represent an empty log
read. Displayed timestamp/process/message aliases accept text, finite numbers or
absent values. Nested values and malformed arrays are unavailable, never rendered
as React objects or treated as empty success. The OPNsense __timestamp__ alias is
used consistently for both display and sorting. Log strings remain escaped text.

The selected table is hidden while fetching, after a failed read and when its
cached response does not match the gateway/vendor. A generic unavailable message
does not reflect vendor diagnostics. Retry reads only the selected log endpoint.
React Query keys remain scoped to the gateway and log kind; late responses from a
previous gateway must not populate the current table. Previously displayed data
cannot be recalled. This change does not implement durable log storage, new log
vendor mappings, background streaming or real-device authentication acceptance.

The correction is checked on the actual gateway page with synthetic API responses,
and independently in Chromium using the actual Axios client over loopback HTTP.
This is browser/query/response-contract coverage, not production hardware evidence.
The English, Spanish and Chinese availability strings and earlier missing health,
certificate-warning, backup-comparison and OpenVPN-profile translations retain the
existing full namespace/key/interpolation verification gate.
